            {
                "entry_id": "df52d2b2-f661-3d9c-b913-6b5ea7d41c88",
                "word": "Acheron",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ec83f39a-bcaa-3d28-8ad5-b92d20d78ae8",
                        "entry_id": "df52d2b2-f661-3d9c-b913-6b5ea7d41c88",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A river in the infernal regions; also, the infernal regions themselves. By some of the English poets, it was supposed to be a flaming lake or gulf."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Greek"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e9ae046-fd19-4714-9f7c-1490bda1e0d0",
                                "sense_id": "ec83f39a-bcaa-3d28-8ad5-b92d20d78ae8",
                                "text": "And pull her out of Acheron by the heels"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2540da38-1d09-4b7b-b18c-904f02d50c67",
                                "sense_id": "ec83f39a-bcaa-3d28-8ad5-b92d20d78ae8",
                                "text": "Acheron and Phlegeton, which a subterraneous fire causes to boil, are the billows of that hell which was visited by Æneas."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c78ec65-238a-4ac9-b261-77803aec05ad",
                                "sense_id": "ec83f39a-bcaa-3d28-8ad5-b92d20d78ae8",
                                "text": "Behold! I rise from primal silence / As a storm crushing dismal shores ov Acheron"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "84c7505b-0246-3936-8ae4-53786edffc44",
                        "entry_id": "df52d2b2-f661-3d9c-b913-6b5ea7d41c88",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Hell"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d4b716a2-f3f9-3830-985f-92fbef5ce289",
                        "entry_id": "df52d2b2-f661-3d9c-b913-6b5ea7d41c88",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A small town in Victoria, Australia."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "584b11c3-0958-49ba-bd15-db448fdddfac",
                        "source_entry_id": "df52d2b2-f661-3d9c-b913-6b5ea7d41c88",
                        "source_sense_description": "a river",
                        "target_lang_word": "Achéron",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Achéron",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c4fcc603-1d36-3bfb-8157-726058c187be",
                                        "entry_id": "2c39759f-64ae-390f-acc2-b552f0ec0614",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fleuve des Enfers grecs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26900819-fc18-4f71-9c1f-d68f1c215e47",
                                                "sense_id": "c4fcc603-1d36-3bfb-8157-726058c187be",
                                                "text": "Dans la deuxième partie sont tous les coupables, qui s’empressent de passer le fleuve Achéron dans la barque du nautonier des Enfers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf902ff7-44c9-4f01-99f7-cf355e197d44",
                                                "sense_id": "c4fcc603-1d36-3bfb-8157-726058c187be",
                                                "text": "En bas, ce n’était plus le Lot qui coulait, mais le fleuve des Enfers, l’Achéron."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "701b201f-6f76-4085-b3b6-4d9463762c63",
                                                "sense_id": "c4fcc603-1d36-3bfb-8157-726058c187be",
                                                "text": "Lucrèce, dans son troisième livre, entreprend de chasser des cœurs « cette crainte de l’Achéron qui trouble jusqu’au fond de la vie humaine »."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cff953a7-13bc-3713-9c82-a864143e284a",
                                        "entry_id": "2c39759f-64ae-390f-acc2-b552f0ec0614",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "L’enfer ; la mort."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "poetic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0bdaad40-c564-4594-ae57-a439a1be6dd5",
                                                "sense_id": "cff953a7-13bc-3713-9c82-a864143e284a",
                                                "text": "Un mal qui répand la terreur […]\nLa peste, puisqu’il faut l’appeler par son nom,\nCapable d’enrichir en un jour l’Achéron."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bd894c3c-f9c8-3c7d-95df-566e81db61bd",
                                        "entry_id": "2c39759f-64ae-390f-acc2-b552f0ec0614",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dans l’univers fictif de Conan, créé par Robert E. Howard, le royaume disparu d’Achéron correspond à l’Empire romain. Son territoire couvrait l’Aquilonie, la Némédie et Argos."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
